---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  <code>wc-chat-thread</code> holds a conversation's <code>wc-chat-message</code>s, oldest first. It
  fills its container and scrolls, keeping the latest message in view while the person reads the end.
  Scroll up in the demo and a <strong>Jump to latest</strong> button appears.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-chat-thread style='block-size: 20rem; inline-size: 100%; max-inline-size: 30rem; border: 1px solid var(--color-outline-variant); border-radius: var(--shape-corner-medium);'>
    <wc-chat-message from='user' value='What is waiting for me?'></wc-chat-message>
    <wc-chat-message value='Two things need you today: **Ada asked for your timesheet**, and INC-2318 is waiting for your reply.'></wc-chat-message>
    <wc-chat-message from='user' value='Remind me about the timesheet at 4.'></wc-chat-message>
    <wc-chat-message value='Done. I set a reminder for 16:00 in your calendar.'></wc-chat-message>
    <wc-chat-message from='user' value='And the incident?'></wc-chat-message>
    <wc-chat-message value='INC-2318 is about the cracked screen on LT-0412. Desk support asked when you can bring the laptop in.'></wc-chat-message>
  </wc-chat-thread>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Before the first message</h3>
<p>
  The <code>empty</code> slot and <code>suggestions</code> show until the first message: prompt
  starters as chips that fire <code>suggestion-select</code>.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-chat-thread id='thread-empty' style='inline-size: 100%; max-inline-size: 30rem;'>
    <p slot='empty'>What can I help with?</p>
  </wc-chat-thread>
  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var thread = document.querySelector('#thread-empty');
      thread.suggestions = ['Request leave', 'Report a problem', "What's waiting for me?"];
      thread.addEventListener('suggestion-select', function (event) {
        myConsole.log('suggestion-select: ' + event.detail.value);
      });
    })();
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Accessibility</h3>
<p>
  The thread is a log (<code>role="log"</code>) named "Conversation", but not a live region: a
  streaming answer would be read word by word. Instead it announces each assistant answer once, when
  its <code>streaming</code> turns off, as "Assistant: …" (the <code>chatAnnouncement</code> string).
  Messages already there when the thread connects, and the person's own messages, are not announced.
</p>
